# Database Migrations

## Project Setup

### 1. Configure database URL

Set the DB_URL in .env

### 2. Apply all migrations

```bash
uv run alembic upgrade head
```

---

## Making Model Changes

Whenever you add, remove, or modify a model, follow this workflow:

### 1. Make your changes

Edit the relevant file(s) under `src/repositories/models/`.

### 2. Generate a migration

```bash
uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "short description of change"
```

A new file will appear in `migrations/versions/`. **Open it and review** the `upgrade()` and `downgrade()` functions before continuing.

> [!WARNING]
> Autogenerate doesn't catch everything - renames, custom constraints, and some index changes may need to be written manually.

### 3. Apply the migration

```bash
uv run alembic upgrade head
```

### 4. Commit the migration file

The generated file must be committed alongside your model change so other developers can pick it up with `alembic upgrade head`.

```bash
git add migrations/versions/
git commit -m "migration: short description of change"
```